  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Big River** (1 review): Reviewer calls this one of the best versions of the song they have heard [10]\n- **He's Gone** (1 review): Reviewer urges listening to this version of the song at least once [5]\n- **One More Saturday Night** (1 review): Reviewer liked that the show closed with this song [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd80-08-23.aud.gillis.11928.sbeok.shnf** (recommended): audience recording; 20 songs; 145 min; rated 2.4/5 by 5 [1]. Said about its sound: Instrument separation is weak and mics were too distant, but the recording conveys Alpine Valley's heavy energy and momentum; loud playback rocks; Reviewer feels their older cassette copy sounds better than this audience recording; Played at full volume, the recording feels just like being there, according to this reviewer [3][4][8][10]\n- **gd1980-08-23.aud.miller.89130.sbeok.flac16**: audience recording; 20 songs; 149 min; rated 1.67/5 by 3 [2]. Said about its sound: Audience recording has a fair amount of crowd noise but still sounds great to this reviewer; This Charlie Miller recording has painfully excessive high end; Uploader says the source is far from great but better than the other circulating source [2][5][9]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer grew up 30 minutes from Alpine and attended just before leaving for freshman year in Madison [6]\n- Alabama Getaway turned up in about 58% of 1980 shows, according to the reviewer's statistics [7]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd80-08-23.aud.gillis.11928.sbeok.shnf**: source: Audience Recording [1]. Also: Unknown equipment to cassette to CDR; Glenn Gillis seeded it to etree [1]\n- **gd1980-08-23.aud.miller.89130.sbeok.flac16**: transferred by Charlie Miller; source: Unknown Mics -> Cassette Master -> Cassette [2]. Also: Tapes came from Joani Walker and Paul Scotton [2]",
